-- THIRD measured cell, NOT run by this gate (same reason order-swapped.mdk isn't
-- run by the sibling ../1351-methoddispatchidx-import-order-collision/ fixture --
-- diff_compiler_must_fail.sh grades exactly one `cmd:` plus one `control:`). Kept
-- here for traceability of the causal-variable claim in claim.txt.
--
-- Same graph as main.mdk/control.mdk, but zmodI's member list names only `zf`, NOT
-- `IZ` -- so `IZ` is UNADMITTED (S1-NS (a) never sees it) while `impl IZ String`
-- remains present in the compiled graph. Measured: `medaka run iz-unadmitted.mdk`
-- -> 7, exit 0 -- IDENTICAL to main.mdk's two-admitted cell, despite IZ itself
-- being unadmitted here. This is what shows the causal variable is the GRAPH
-- PRESENCE of `impl IZ String`, not whether IZ's own declaration is admitted --
-- an S2-DECL (c) question (`implExistsForHead` is keyed by method name + head
-- tycon, never by interface, so it can answer about an impl of a declaration `M`
-- cannot even name), not (b). See claim.txt's three-cell table.
import fmodI.{mth}
import amodI.{IA, af}
import zmodI.{zf}

main = println (mth "abc" 5 + af 0 + zf 0)
